The rule for conformance.kernel.recovery states: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text" [65ae18af7a738b26]. However, fence content must parse as JSON to be scored directly from the fence. In the input constructed from cell fence[ A S ] fence[ B ], the first fence contains object A followed by sentence S, making it unparseable as strict JSON. The second fence contains only object B, which parses successfully. Since fences are tried in reverse order, B is scored as the last parseable fence object. In the rewritten text, the second fence block containing B is removed, leaving only fence[ A S ]. Since that fence contains prose and won't parse, recovery falls back to finding top-level objects, extracting A from within the fence content. Therefore, the recovered object moves from B to A.